Have a microphone's options set the voice engine's audio processing

In M156 a channel's AudioOptions no longer reach the audio processing
(WebRtcVoiceSendChannel::SetOptions only keeps them): WebRTC's own factory applies them
as global options when it makes an audio source (PeerConnectionFactory::CreateAudioSource,
ConnectionContext::ApplyGlobalAudioOptions, kept and applied once the engine starts). The
wrapper makes its sources itself and never did, so the processing kept the engine's
defaults (echo cancelling, gain control, noise suppression at its highest level and the
high-pass filter, all on) whatever the application asked. A microphone source's options
now go through the factory's CreateAudioSource, whose source is not used; a custom
source's (a shared screen's sound, which never goes through the processing) never do.

diff --git a/src/rtc_peerconnection_factory_impl.cc b/src/rtc_peerconnection_factory_impl.cc
index 3588ad4..38af33c 100644
--- a/src/rtc_peerconnection_factory_impl.cc
+++ b/src/rtc_peerconnection_factory_impl.cc
@@ -255,6 +255,18 @@ scoped_refptr<RTCAudioSource> RTCPeerConnectionFactoryImpl::CreateAudioSource(
   rtc_options.auto_gain_control = options.auto_gain_control;
   rtc_options.noise_suppression = options.noise_suppression;
   rtc_options.highpass_filter = options.highpass_filter;
+  // Fogata: a microphone's options set the voice engine's one audio processing, as
+  // WebRTC's own factory does when it makes an audio source (it keeps them as global
+  // options, applied at once or when the engine starts). The wrapper makes its
+  // sources itself and never did: the processing kept the engine's defaults (noise
+  // suppression and the high-pass filter on) whatever the application asked. Only
+  // through the factory's CreateAudioSource can they reach the engine; the source it
+  // makes is not used. Never a custom source's (a shared screen's sound), which never
+  // goes through the processing and must not change the microphone's.
+  if (source_type == RTCAudioSource::SourceType::kMicrophone &&
+      rtc_peerconnection_factory_) {
+    rtc_peerconnection_factory_->CreateAudioSource(rtc_options);
+  }
   webrtc::scoped_refptr<libwebrtc::LocalAudioSource> rtc_source_track =
       CreateAudioSourceWithOptions(
           &rtc_options, source_type == RTCAudioSource::SourceType::kCustom);
